# GROUP_ID course group — one line stating this group's combination intent

> **Status**: planned / a preparatory course group
>
> **Pointer**: memory "Current state pointers" → `Course group:GROUP_ID` → this file.
> **Calendar**: `main/30_group/GROUP_ID/calendar.md`; this file owns only the member combination, the
> activation gate, and the capacity boundary.
>
> **Position**: one line saying whether this group is the current execution window or a draft of the next
> one. A planned group does not change the current course-group pointer in
> `t2ag_memory.md`, and does not change any member course's lifecycle.
>
> **Authority boundary**: this file describes the combination intent only. Each course's progress is still
> governed solely by its own `progress.md`; a course in the planned state is changed only when this group
> is activated.

---

## 1. Activation conditions

This group becomes active only once all of the following hold:

1. Every closing-evidence item in the previous group's `review.md` is ticked.
2. Every decidable threshold in the previous group's `calendar.md` is met.
3. Every non-course member has verifiable entry evidence; without evidence it is removed from the members
   rather than treating a wish as a condition.
4. This group's concrete budget is written into `calendar.md` and has passed the overload review.
5. The user explicitly chooses to enter this group, rather than extending the previous one or switching to
   another combination.

