## 3. Capacity boundary

- Frequency red line: each member's minimum count per cycle; failing to reach it is overload.
- Time budget: total hours per cycle and their allocation; the actual deviation is recorded in `review.md`.
- Overload handling: lower the frequency of non-red-line members first and never cut the red line first;
  two consecutive cycles below target trigger a review of the whole combination.

---

## 4. Keystone sequence (required for a `progress` group; a `schedule` group has no such section — the generator deletes it by mode)

> The planned stage holds a draft; the freeze happens at activation (the group-forming ritual). The
> machine entry point is `t2ag_init.py activate-group`: it verifies that this table already holds real
> keystone rows (a remaining `keystone description` placeholder is refused), counts them, and writes
> `keystone_total_frozen: N` into the frontmatter (N = the number of rows below). The anchor is never
> written by hand.
> Once frozen, the only entry for cutting a keystone is the ledger in the next section
> (`course_group_rules.md` §4.3); doctor reconciles: current keystones + logged cut rows = the anchor.

- K01 keystone description (which course it belongs to, and which line of that course's progress.md its completion criterion points at)
- K02 keystone description

